===Etymology===
From {{der|en|frm|chiromancie}}, from {{der|en|la|chīromantīa}}, from {{der|en|grc|χειρομαντεία}}, from {{m|grc|χειρο-||[[hand]]-}} + {{m|grc|μαντεία||[[divination]], [[fortune-telling]]}}. Equivalent to {{confix|en|chiro|mancy}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkaɪ.ɹəʊ.mæn.si/|/ˈkaɪ.ɹə.mæn.si/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|+}}

# {{synonym of|en|palmistry}}: [[fortune-telling]] [[perform]]ed by [[reading]] [[another]]'s [[hand]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1620|author=J. Melton Astrologaster
|passage=If they fore-tell things that shall happen by signes that they see in lines of a mans hand; then it is called Chyromancie...}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1995|author=C. Walker Encyc|title=Secret Knowledge
|passage=Modern palmistry differs from the ancient methods in concentrating on what is called chirognomy at the expense of '''chiromancy'''.}}

